    {
      "id": "e174",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 677,
      "width": 406.4985790002389,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046600,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. TBB conductor sizing (TIA-607-D, by run length): up to\n13 ft = #6; 14–20 ft = #4; 21–26 ft = #3; 27–33 ft = #2;\n34–41 ft = #1; 42–52 ft = 1/0; 53–66 ft = 2/0; over 66 ft\n= 3/0 AWG.",
      "originalText": "1. TBB conductor sizing (TIA-607-D, by run length): up to 13 ft = #6; 14–20 ft = #4; 21–26 ft = #3; 27–33 ft = #2; 34–41 ft = #1; 42–52 ft = 1/0; 53–66 ft = 2/0; over 66 ft = 3/0 AWG.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 140,
      "versionNonce": 1782361094,
      "index": "b01",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e175",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 748,
      "width": 406.49884673998025,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Rack bonding conductor: #6 AWG stranded copper from\neach rack to the TGB. Home-run each rack; do not daisy-\nchain.",
      "originalText": "2. Rack bonding conductor: #6 AWG stranded copper from each rack to the TGB. Home-run each rack; do not daisy-chain.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 160,
      "versionNonce": 1714978650,
      "index": "b02",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e176",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 406.49884673998025,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Bond both ends of every cable tray run and jumper\nacross every splice plate. Splice plates are a mechanical\njoint, not an electrical one.",
      "originalText": "3. Bond both ends of every cable tray run and jumper across every splice plate. Splice plates are a mechanical joint, not an electrical one.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 177,
      "versionNonce": 387267398,
      "index": "b03",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e177",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 412.18523723506024,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. The equipment grounding conductor in each branch\ncircuit is separate from, and additional to, the telecom\nbonding system. Neither replaces the other.",
      "originalText": "4. The equipment grounding conductor in each branch circuit is separate from, and additional to, the telecom bonding system. Neither replaces the other.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 184,
      "versionNonce": 2086896666,
      "index": "b04",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e178",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 910,
      "width": 399.99999999999994,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. Never drive an isolated ground rod for the server\nroom. Two electrodes at different potentials, bonded\nonly through your equipment, is how you destroy switch\nports in a lightning event.",
      "originalText": "5. Never drive an isolated ground rod for the server room. Two electrodes at different potentials, bonded only through your equipment, is how you destroy switch ports in a lightning event.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 295,
      "versionNonce": 278520454,
      "index": "b05",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e179",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 979,
      "width": 402.4369671250898,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786231046601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Test and record: bond continuity < 1 ohm to the TGB,\nand the electrode system per the local requirement\n(commonly ≤ 25 ohms, or ≤ 5 ohms where the owner\nspecifies it).",
      "originalText": "6. Test and record: bond continuity < 1 ohm to the TGB, and the electrode system per the local requirement (commonly ≤ 25 ohms, or ≤ 5 ohms where the owner specifies it).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 201,
      "versionNonce": 1213198554,
      "index": "b06",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
